      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Compare the final directions. The river-bank occurrence is now more aligned with the river clue than with money. The financial occurrence shows the reverse relation. Each result can be checked from the displayed coordinates and the exact weighted updates used in this fixture.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 15.736,
          "duration": 15.336,
          "until": 16.336
        },
        {
          "say": "The embedding table still contains one bank row. Contextualization changed the state of each occurrence during the forward pass, so storing separate vocabulary entries for every possible sentence was unnecessary. The same learned machinery can respond differently when its available context changes.",
          "start": 16.336,
          "end": 34.072,
          "duration": 17.736,
          "until": 34.672
        },
        {
          "say": "A word split into several subword tokens introduces another representation choice. You might inspect one subtoken state, combine several states, or pool a whole sentence, depending on the task. Keep that choice explicit when comparing vectors, because different pooling rules answer different questions.",
          "start": 34.672,
          "end": 53.224,
          "duration": 18.552,
